 ## Background
-Mipmap filtering was introduced as a solution to texture aliasing in computer graphics, based on the Nyquist–Shannon sampling theorem [S1, unofficial]. It is a standard technique in physically-based rendering, often used in conjunction with solving the light transport equation [S1, unofficial]. The concept has been extended to 3D volumes and sparse voxel structures, such as Sparse Volume Textures (SVT) in Unreal Engine [S2].
